1. What does "x" mean?

When you open a file using "x", Python tries to create a brand-new file.

with open("newfile.txt", "x") as file:
    file.write("I am learning Python.")
What happens?

If newfile.txt does not exist, Python creates it and writes the text.

If newfile.txt already exists, Python raises a FileExistsError.

Python does not overwrite the existing file.

