3. What if the file already exists?

Suppose you run the same code again:

with open("example.txt", "x") as file:
    file.write("Another text")

Python will produce this error:

FileExistsError: [Errno 17] File exists: 'example.txt'

Why? Because "x" is designed to create a new file and prevent accidental overwriting.